---
source: gate/src/checks/tests.rs
expression: render_list()
---
CHECK             REACH      TRIGGER (hook, quick)
pending-snapshots hook       always
                             no insta `.snap.new` is staged (hook) or tracked
rustfmt           hook       **/*.rs
                             the workspace, the nine guests and the four fixtures (the bridge component included) are rustfmt-clean
spec-format       hook       computed: a .spec file in a project's spec dir; the formatter, parser or grammar
                             the .spec files of every project are formatted
grammar           hook       crates/kernel/tree-sitter/grammar.js, crates/kernel/tree-sitter/src/**
                             the committed tree-sitter artifacts are what grammar.js generates
zero-entity       hook       crates/**/src/**, scripts/check-zero-entity-core.sh
                             the core crates name no entity kind of an extension
layers            hook       Cargo.toml, crates/**/Cargo.toml, gate/src/layers.rs
                             no crate has a normal or build dependency on a crate in a higher layer (its folder under crates/) or in none
links             hook       computed: a .spec file; a test file or one with a `verify =` attribute
                             every test's verify text and entity is declared by the spec (A016, static)
doc-links         hook       always
                             every relative link in a tracked Markdown file names a tracked file or directory
root-layout       hook       always
                             the tracked top-level entries are the root list's (gate/src/root_layout.rs)
builtins          quick      computed: a file some blob's inputs.json records
                             every committed blob was built from the sources it recorded
guests            quick      extensions/**, crates/**, integrations/rust/**, Cargo.toml
                             each guest's tests pass and it is clippy-clean for wasm and native
audit             quick      **/Cargo.lock
                             no lockfile holds an unsound or yanked dependency
build             quick      computed: a workspace member; the root manifest, lockfile or nextest config [compiles]
                             every workspace test binary and the CLI build
tests             quick      computed: a workspace member; the root manifest, lockfile or nextest config (after build)
                             the workspace tests pass (quick: the changed crates and their dependents)
clippy            quick      crates/**, integrations/rust/**, xtask/**, gate/**, Cargo.toml, Cargo.lock, clippy.toml [compiles]
                             the workspace is clippy-clean with warnings denied
doctests          quick      computed: a workspace member that holds a runnable doctest (after build)
                             the doctests of the crates that have one pass
published-schemas quick      **/*.spec, **/specforge.json, extensions/**, crates/pipeline/emitter/**, crates/pipeline/graph/**, crates/pipeline/registry/**, crates/app/ops/tests/operations/schema.rs (after build)
                             every project's exports validate against the schema `specforge schema --publish` prints for their format
specs             quick      **/*.spec, **/specforge.json, gate/baseline.json, extensions/**, crates/**/src/**, crates/**/Cargo.toml
                             every project checks with no error and no warning above the baseline
dogfood           full       always (after tests, guests)
                             the tests' reports leave no unknown entity (W115), failing proof (A014) or undeclared obligation (A016)
builtins-verify   bootstrap  always
                             a cold clone rebuilds every committed blob to the vendored bytes
